{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh took off his ring from his hand</b> — The giving of the king's ring is a sign for the one who receives it that he is to be second to him in greatness; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 41:42). But the correct interpretation is that the king's ring is his seal, as in the matter of \"and seal it with the king's ring\" (Esther 8:8). So he gave him the seal to be ruler and commander over the entire kingdom, and to seal with the king's ring whatever he desires."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:22:18.417755198Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}